WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.419
The takeaway: for vision transformers,

00:00:02.499 --> 00:00:06.233
you need not trade accuracy for privacy in split learning.

00:00:06.313 --> 00:00:11.823
Adding Gaussian noise and mixing randomly masked
patches across clients amplifies the

00:00:11.903 --> 00:00:16.886
differential-privacy guarantee over plain split
learning and raises accuracy,

00:00:16.966 --> 00:00:20.240
with the gain provably bounded by a Mixup baseline.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:25.172
It works because transformers use global
self-attention at the patch level,

00:00:25.252 --> 00:00:29.184
so swapping patches costs little, though it would
hurt a CNN.

00:00:29.264 --> 00:00:34.050
Patch-level CutMix is a privacy regularizer built
for the transformer era.
